{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791688132,"nonce":"tt4xwlt4INkTwRTEmCRELlYtdkc=","message":"Decision: base image digests are an all-zero sha256 placeholder (64 zeros) because the worker had no network or podman and will not invent digests. scripts/pin-image-digests.sh resolves tags to real digests via skopeo or podman and rewrites the FROM lines; --check fails while placeholders remain; the C8 CI job runs it for the build when placeholders remain. Reason: a pinned-looking fake digest would fail every build, an unpinned FROM would break the spec rule. Maintainer must run the script once and commit as chore:. Decision: uv image tag 0.12.5 (version installed in the dev environment) must be confirmed on first pin. Decision: .containerignore also excludes scripts, examples, extension, .github and *.key beyond the ticket list since the image copies only pyproject.toml, uv.lock, README.md and src. Decision: the ignore-matcher in tests/test_containerfile.py reimplements docker pattern semantics (** spans dirs, parent match excludes children) and also asserts no real src file is excluded. Verified: uv build --wheel in a temp dir with only pyproject.toml uv.lock README.md src succeeds; without README.md it fails. Only CI or a host can verify the image build, size, and the unconfirmed uv tag.","files":null}]}